{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.GaussianTiltedSum","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.GaussianTiltedSum","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.GaussianThetaBound"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.tsum_tilted_gaussian_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.tsum_tilted_gaussian_pos","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/GaussianTiltedSum.lean#L94-L101","doc":"The tilted sum is positive — needed to divide by it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.sum_le_tsum_tilted_gaussian","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.sum_le_tsum_tilted_gaussian","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/GaussianTiltedSum.lean#L87-L92","doc":"Any finite part of the tilted sum is at most the whole — the free half of\nthe window-versus-`ℤ` comparison.  (The other half needs a tail bound.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.abs_tsum_tilted_gaussian_sub_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.abs_tsum_tilted_gaussian_sub_le","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/GaussianTiltedSum.lean#L51-L85","doc":"**The tilted sum equals the tilted integral**, up to the same\nexponentially small relative error as the untilted one.\n\n`e^{L²/a}·√(π/a)` is exactly `∫_ℝ e^{−ax² + 2Lx} dx`, so this says the tilted\nLaplace sum is its tilted Laplace integral — which is the statement the\nconstant `c_σ` is read off from. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.summable_tilted_gaussian","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.summable_tilted_gaussian","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/GaussianTiltedSum.lean#L40-L49","doc":"The tilted family is summable over `ℤ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.exp_quadratic_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.exp_quadratic_eq","kind":"theorem","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/GaussianTiltedSum.lean#L30-L38","doc":"**Completing the square.**  A linear tilt is a shift of the centre plus a\nconstant factor. ","signatureChunk":0}]}